<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Liaodong (206 BC)</h1><p class="st-meta">206 BCE – 206 BCE · capital Wuzhong</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A remote north-eastern kingdom given to the deposed Yan king Han Guang in 206 BCE, who was killed within months for refusing to leave his old realm.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-guang">Han Guang</a>, once a commander sent north by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-chen">Wu Chen</a>, the rebel king of Zhao, had made himself king of Yan during the rising against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a>. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu's</a> settlement of 206 BCE he was demoted to King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a>, a distant territory beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-river">Liao River</a> with its capital at Wuzhong, while his general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zang-tu">Zang Tu</a> received Yan.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-guang">Han Guang</a> refused to give up Yan and move to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a>, so the kingdom hardly functioned as a separate state.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Later in 206 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zang-tu">Zang Tu</a> attacked and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-guang">Han Guang</a> at Wuzhong and annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> to Yan (206 BC).</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 206 BCE – 206 BCE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:55.60%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>206 BCE – 206 BCE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Wuzhong</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Han Guang</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese ancestral religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>China</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Liaodong (Han Guang)</dd></dl></aside></div>

